# Uploaded document files live under here. They must NEVER be served
# directly by the web server — every legitimate read goes through
# actions/download_document.php, which enforces the same matter-access RBAC
# (ethical walls, confidentiality tiers, assignment) as the rest of the app
# and writes an audit record. Without this file, once this project is
# deployed under Apache's document root (see README setup), anyone who
# guessed or observed a storage path could fetch a confidential document
# directly, bypassing RBAC entirely — and an uploaded .php file would be
# *executed* by Apache rather than just served as a static file, since
# storage/ sits inside the web root.
#
# Apache 2.4+ (this project's documented XAMPP target):
<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    Require all denied
</IfModule>
# Apache 2.2 and earlier fallback:
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
    Order deny,allow
    Deny from all
</IfModule>
